From: Pingouin
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: Pingouin's boot splash, the icon's penguin against a turning glow

What: the boot splash of pingouin-cocoa-boot-splash.patch shows the app
icon's penguin, huge and black (2.25 x the output's height), framed as in
the icon so its head and neck show, against a soft glow of the icon's six
colours on near-black; the glow turns slowly behind it (one lap in 25 s,
still with macOS's Reduce motion), instead of Omarchy's logo. It is on by
default again (PINGOUIN_BOOT_SPLASH=0 turns it off). The rest is upstream's:
it holds over the firmware, GRUB and Linux's console until the desktop is
lit, then fades; black once the desktop turned an output off; the
slow-start hint, now white, near the bottom.
How: pingouin_splash_pixels draws the still splash with Core Graphics at the
output's size in pixels; the GL layers and the IOSurface path blit it as a
texture made at that size. The overlay layer is the grey, the glow (an image
the size of the diagonal, turned by Core Animation) and the penguin (a shape
layer). Colours are tagged with the window's colour space (GL's pixels show
unconverted). The penguin is a vector outline in ui/pingouin-splash-art.h,
traced from app/Resources/icon/penguin.png by runtime/tools/trace-penguin.py.
Upstream: Pingouin only (branding).
